# `npm run replay:run` writes its replayed state log beside the golden it is compared against, so
# that `replay:diff --actual` can find it. It is scratch: the golden is `expected.ndjson` and it is
# only ever written by `replay:run --accept` (the golden-update protocol). Ignoring the scratch file
# is what keeps an ordinary developer run from dirtying a committed session directory — and keeps a
# mistyped `--accept` from being the thing that promotes it.
fixtures/sessions/*/actual.ndjson
